# The NDJSON logs are append-only, and two runs appending from divergent
# bases is a textbook add/add conflict at end-of-file -- verified, not
# assumed. A plain rebase stops with conflict markers in exactly the
# situation the rebase exists to handle.
#
# Union takes both sides' lines. That is correct here precisely because
# these files are append-only and every line is a self-contained record
# carrying its own run_date: no line depends on its neighbours, so
# interleaving is harmless and nothing is lost.
log/*.ndjson merge=union
